<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia's BDET bank has higher '96 profits.</title>
<headline>Tunisia's BDET bank has higher '96 profits.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque de Developpement Economique de Tunisie net profits were 6.674 million dinars in 1996, up from 5.550 million dinars in 1995, results showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The state-controlled bank is specialised in loans for development projects.</p>
<p>It has a capital of 50.5 million dinars and reserves were 30.862 million dinars at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>BDET is listed at the Tunis Stock Exchange. Its share was last priced at 15.15 dinars. ($=1.08 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
